{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game","id":806305,"title":"Ideas for using Changelins in W:tA game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-11T12:08:03-08:00","id":806305,"title":"Ideas for using Changelins in W:tA game","content":"Hello, I've been running a W:tA game for over 2 years. I've had my characters deal with fomori, demons, vampires, spirits, Pentex etc. I am wanting to have them involved with something different. That is why I am posting this here. I have had a thread through the story for eventually having the pack get involved with Changelings So I thought I'd ask for some ideas here. Any help would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> The story so far is the pack are high school students. The Ragabash has a 'girl friend' that just happens to be Kinain. They met her when they started at the school. She is the prettiest girl in school. The actually met her when she was being hit on by the quarterback of the football team. She didn't like him, he is also Garou and is an Ahroun, so that really turn her off. She latched on to one of the PCs saying this is my boyfriend to keep the QB away. This was a thing for convince, she let the player know and they worked it out to mess with the QB. Later, the packs Ragabash started to hit on her since she didn't seem to be interested in any of the guys. So they became a thing. Of course this lead to a lot of amusing things in school. Anyway, the Ragabash found out that her girlfriend was actually a guy (still the prettiest girl at school). Kim is her name. The Galliard in the pack has figured out some, but the Ragabash knows the most but not all of Kim's back ground.<br /> <br /> Kim is Kinain, his mother is a noble Sidhe, and his father is a Unseelie Pooka knight. Neither of his parents families wanted them to marry or have kids. Kim is the oldest child, he's 16, he has a younger brother, age 12, a fox pooka. He used to have a middle sister, but she was been killed when Kim was 10 and that's when he and his brother went into hiding. Kim has very strong Fae blood but isn't Fae. He has fae blood background of 5, parted mists, honored birthright (both pooka and sidhe). He has fae marks (pointed ears and cat eyes). Some of his family has been helping him and his brother to hid. Kim took on a female persona to help( he's been living as a girl for 6 years now). Kim and his brother have been moving around to keep them safe. The game is set in Eastern Kentucky, Kim moved there about 4 months before school started. His brother was sent to live with him after a few months. As I said, the pack doesn't really know much about Kim's background.<br /> <br /> What I was thinking about, was having Kim's brother kidnapped and Kim having to go back home to Ireland and try to find him. Of course, his girlfriend and her pack would go along to help. So any ideas would be useful. Also, ask any questions about Kim and his background also if you need more information. I don't know a lot about changeling, as I've never had the chance to play even though I own most of the books. <br /> <br /> Thanks again for ay help or ideas. I'd like to flesh out this adventure and make it something special.<br /> <br /> David<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:53:11-08:00","id":806351,"title":"","content":"House Balor is pretty much inherently Wyrm tainted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T12:55:43-08:00","id":806358,"title":"","content":"Not really tied directly to what you've got so far, but House Fiana of the Sidhe is known for having a close relationship with one of the Werewolf Clans. So that's another possible hook. Perhaps Kim needs help from House Fiana and thinks a werewolf escort would improve his reception?<br /> <br /> Before having Kim's brother kidnapped, perhaps have him play a bit more of a role in the game in a slice-of-life sort of way. Have him, maybe, even pretend to be a Kitsune Changing Breed as he doesn't want to admit being a Changeling (being in hiding and all) and use that as a reason to hang out with the &quot;cool kids&quot; his older brother's always hanging around. If the PCs have younger siblings or friends, let the little brother be involved with them.<br /> <br /> The more you can give the little brother some personal attachment to the PCs - that is, have them care about the kid for his own sake - the more the pack will want to help Kim out for reasons beyond &quot;drop everything for the Ragabash's girlie boyfriend.&quot; Remember that pooka are tricksters; use that as you see fit, but try not to let it make the kid antagonistic or annoying to the PCs. Is the kid Seelie or unSeelie?<br /> <br /> <br /> Unrelated random thought: Have the pooka kid think he's &quot;too grown up&quot; for stuffed animals anymore, but one of his favorite toys from when he was younger be something dog-ish or wolf-ish. Now that he's &quot;discarded&quot; it, a chimera that grew into it from his attachment to it is lonely, jealous, and trying to get his attention again. So now a chimerical werewolf is alternately trying to &quot;be his friend&quot; and stalk him, helping him make friends with the local pack(s) of younger were-kids and/or hunting and terrorizing him. Either way, that might get the party's attention as an initial introduction. If it's not a hostile chimera, maybe the PCs even meet it and mistake it for a real Garou at first, learning the truth only later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:03:28-08:00","id":806368,"title":"","content":"Fiona, and garou have tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:33:41-08:00","id":806419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=806368#post806368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fiona, and garou have tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, sorry. So it's the Fiana Tribe of Garou with which House Fiona is (vaguely) allied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T14:44:35-08:00","id":806482,"title":"","content":"Thanks for some of the ideas. Kim's brother has already meet the PCs. In fact he's currently in a prank war with Kim's girlfriend, the Ragabash. Nothing serious so far, but he's keeping her on her toes. Also, Kim's brother got the pack Ahroun to swear an oath to protect him from anything that would want to harm him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T13:24:41-08:00","id":807255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=806419#post806419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, sorry. So it's the Fiana Tribe of Garou with which House Fiona is (vaguely) allied.</div> </div> </div> </div>More like they're involved in a torrid affair that goes back and forth from deep and matchless affection to bitter rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T13:41:32-08:00","id":807264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=807255#post807255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More like they're involved in a torrid affair that goes back and forth from deep and matchless affection to bitter rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that we're talking about House Fiona and the Fiana Tribe, isn't that the same thing?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T14:33:23-08:00","id":807306,"title":"","content":"LOL pretty much... uhmmmn how would a Thalain or Balor Sidhe fit into a first team?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T15:21:35-08:00","id":808275,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the idea about the chimera Segev, it sounds like a really cool plot thread. But, if Kim's brother is kidnapped, and Kim needs to go back home to Ireland, what would the group encounter? I need ideas for this. My thoughts are some sort of courtly setting. Kim and his brother are of House Fiona. I've never been good a describing any type of courtly type of political maneuverings and really need help. Thanks again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T08:38:35-08:00","id":808732,"title":"","content":"Well, House Fiona are kind-of the &quot;frat boys&quot; of the Sidhe courts, which is part of why they have such a...longstanding...relationship with the Fiana Tribe. Formality is a thing, as they are Seelie, but they throw some of the best and wildest parties that you can manage with high class and beautiful perfection. Like a high-class frat house, they will separate the more crass entertainments into a nearly ritualized decorum, but they will definitely and gleefully indulge in them, and be impressed by them. It's just that you take off your monocle and put on your brawlin' gloves, first.<br /> <br /> Hazing may well be a &quot;thing&quot; that visiting foreign werewolves who are ostensibly allies have to endure, and it may or may not be good-natured (depending on the motives and personalities of the people involved). Both the Fiana and Fiona value a certain amount of spiritual, physical, and social toughness, so it won't be insulting to engage in such behavior with even diplomats, let alone with strangers come to beg a favor. They'll also be big, even for a noble court, on proving yourself and earning the right to ask a favor. It is not at all unreasonable to expect one or more favors-as-quests that the Sidhe might ask of these visiting Garou to earn the right to ask for help. Some of the hazing may even be wound up in this; a snipe hunt is not an unreasonable thing to set as a quest. But if the Garou come through it with good humor and acting strong and worthy and properly respectful (and, at the right times, properly humorously disrespectful), they probably will be welcomed as worthy guests. Unless there's tension between the Garou and Fae at that time and place, in which case things get a LOT harder.<br /> <br /> A lot of what they encounter will depend on who's kidnapped the kid and why, and what their ties (positive or negative) to the local Courts and Houses are. Will the villains be wielding the fae courts as weapons to defend themselves and hinder pursuit, or will they be on the lam from the Changeling powers-that-be, as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:05:13-08:00","id":808797,"title":"","content":"oh would a Goblin or Unseelie Nocker Likely be welcomed into Pentex?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:19:31-08:00","id":808876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=808797#post808797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh would a Goblin or Unseelie Nocker Likely be welcomed into Pentex?</div> </div> </div> </div>No one knows; they'd probably be undone by the sheer volume of paperwork and &quot;it's just the way things are&quot; before anyone even caught on to the character not being human in that capacity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:58:45-08:00","id":808987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=808876#post808876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one knows; they'd probably be undone by the sheer volume of paperwork and &quot;it's just the way things are&quot; before anyone even caught on to the character not being human in that capacity.</div> </div> </div> </div>For all that C:tD makes hay over the Technocracy being inherently Banal, it's really not. The Technocracy is every fantastic story about exciting spy and technological work. While there are elements of banality to it, they're not nearly so overwhelming as is implied by C:tD, which just associated &quot;Banality&quot; with &quot;Badness.&quot; It's a flaw in C:tD that I hope C20 fixes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:03:28-08:00","id":808992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=808987#post808987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For all that C:tD makes hay over the Technocracy being inherently Banal, it's really not. The Technocracy is every fantastic story about exciting spy and technological work. While there are elements of banality to it, they're not nearly so overwhelming as is implied by C:tD, which just associated &quot;Banality&quot; with &quot;Badness.&quot; It's a flaw in C:tD that I hope C20 fixes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't about the Technocracy. This is about Pentex management's unabashed love of making people do paperwork so that they don't have time to think of anything beyond their job. Unlike the Technocracy, it is directly aimed at a banal goal, rather than being just for genuine record-keeping needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:21:05-08:00","id":809017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=808992#post808992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't about the Technocracy. This is about Pentex management's unabashed love of making people do paperwork so that they don't have time to think of anything beyond their job. Unlike the Technocracy, it is directly aimed at a banal goal, rather than being just for genuine record-keeping needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>THen yeah, a nocker who didn't just ignore those rules would be wiped out by banality. (A Dauntain Nocker working for them could be interesting, though.) A Boggan... they're odd, because seemingly-banal tasks are things in which they take great pleasure, making an art out of the perfection and aplomb with which they do them. The Pentex executives would either be thrilled or horrified by the cleanliness, organization, and completeness of all office and paperwork attended by a Boggan, and probably astonished beyond words at how much work they get done overall. Somehow, the Boggan would make it non-banal by making it glamourous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:58:09-08:00","id":809059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=809017#post809017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> THen yeah, a nocker who didn't just ignore those rules would be wiped out by banality. (A Dauntain Nocker working for them could be interesting, though.) A Boggan... they're odd, because seemingly-banal tasks are things in which they take great pleasure, making an art out of the perfection and aplomb with which they do them. The Pentex executives would either be thrilled or horrified by the cleanliness, organization, and completeness of all office and paperwork attended by a Boggan, and probably astonished beyond words at how much work they get done overall. Somehow, the Boggan would make it non-banal by making it glamourous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Horrified, most likely; the entire purpose of Pentex 2100 is to crush anything but the &quot;ant farm&quot; nature of the job. Someone managing to make headway would potentially line themselves up for a TFAA if they kept it up and refused promotions to higher positions that have different, soul-crushing tasks to perform (making other people do the paperwork, cracking the whip to make quota, or possibly even having to oversee the conversion of &quot;test subjects&quot; into fomori.)<br /> <br /> This isn't the Technocracy; they're actually even more banal than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:59:29-08:00","id":809061,"title":"","content":"What does &quot;TFAA&quot; stand for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T15:10:48-08:00","id":809134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=809017#post809017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> THen yeah, a nocker who didn't just ignore those rules would be wiped out by banality. (A Dauntain Nocker working for them could be interesting, though.) A Boggan... they're odd, because seemingly-banal tasks are things in which they take great pleasure, making an art out of the perfection and aplomb with which they do them. The Pentex executives would either be thrilled or horrified by the cleanliness, organization, and completeness of all office and paperwork attended by a Boggan, and probably astonished beyond words at how much work they get done overall. Somehow, the Boggan would make it non-banal by making it glamourous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Unless Pentex had a Project put together they NEEDED the Nocker / Goblin for... remember they current schedule the board of directors meetings around one of their number being a vampire...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T19:03:54-08:00","id":809291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=809061#post809061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does &quot;TFAA&quot; stand for?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tragic, Fiery Automobile Accident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T06:25:35-08:00","id":809542,"title":"","content":"Ahh. How tragic and unpredictable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T23:07:29-08:00","id":810984,"title":"","content":"If you need an interesting way to get the characters to Ireland, changelings have their own version of moonbridges known as &quot;trods&quot;. They're more reliable (and readily accessible) than their werewolf counterparts, but they cut through the Dreaming . . . which means they're governed by fairy tale rules and logic. Good opportunity for a memorable one-shot scenario.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=808987#post808987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For all that C:tD makes hay over the Technocracy being inherently Banal, it's really not. The Technocracy is every fantastic story about exciting spy and technological work. While there are elements of banality to it, they're not nearly so overwhelming as is implied by C:tD, which just associated &quot;Banality&quot; with &quot;Badness.&quot; It's a flaw in C:tD that I hope C20 fixes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with the Technocracy is that there's just no room for changelings in the Technocratic paradigm. Its not that Technocrats are inherently more Banal than humans (or other mages) - the issue is their impact on local consensual reality, actively makes it harder for changelings (or chimera) to exist. Unbelief isn't quite the same thing as Banality . . . .but from a changeling's perspective, its equally toxic.<br /> <br /> As for a nocker working for Pentex . . . .I could see it. There's no reason an evil nocker wouldn't be right at home in R&amp;D, coming up with new ways for humans to hurt themselves (surely that justifies making certain &quot;special accomodations&quot;). And I imagine the higher-ups would love to catch a Seelie nocker in an oath, trapping them into working for the company . . . <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T07:23:53-08:00","id":811098,"title":"","content":"Thing is, while belief is spoken about as a thing for Changelings, the fiction and the rules don't quite bear that out. Changelings don't need to be <i>believed in</i>, they need there to be Glamour in the world, in the form of wonder, hope, aspiration, and dreams. One thing Changelings are <b>not</b> is Tinkerbell; saying &quot;I don't believe in fairies,&quot; doesn't cause one to fall over dead, nor even really hurt them. In fact, ignorance or disbelief can strengthen them if it means that their weaknesses are not invoked. A believer - a superstitious person - might ring his house in salt and iron; one who doesn't believe won't.<br /> <br /> Thus, a nocker or boggan working at Pentex would not be harmed by the disbelief. He would get to be the secret magic faerie that makes things work smoothly, feasting off of any glamour created by the joy of invention (and the dark pleasure of creative murder). What would &quot;get&quot; him, if he wasn't careful, would be the drudgery of the actual day-to-day office work. Every time he was forced to endure a day of tedious, bureaucracy-induced paperwork that got in the way of his actual work, or had his co-workers similarly mired, it would build up banal forces against him.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, that's one area a boggan would outdo a nocker at Pentex: boggans find repetitive but necessary tasks uplifting, and are gifted at their efficient execution (to the point of elevating them out of drudgery and thwarting even deliberate red tape obstacles). They'd thrive on the creativity and productivity of their co-workers as they cleaned up the messes, removed obstacles, and were basically super-administrative assistants who made sure that there was never anything in the way of productive use of everybody else's time.<br /> <br /> A nocker would be in trouble a lot for cutting bureaucratic corners while he just got stuff done, but could potentially also harvest glamour - particularly via ravaging - from the intense frustration and cathartic kvetching sessions of his fellow engineers as they work to get things done in spite of the bureaucracy. Every time he inspired them to throw off a stupid boss's paperwork and get something done, and every time they got away with it because they were just so indispensable, he'd have that dark thrill of smug glamour to sip.<br /> <br /> A nocker and boggan together in one little engineering department could be the best thing to happen to Pentex from a productivity standpoint. It might give the over-bosses, who actually like stifling their own company for some reason, a headache, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T18:08:06-08:00","id":811424,"title":"","content":"One Vorlon, thanks for the idea of using a trod, I forgot about them. One of the things that I was wanting to do was have them have to travel in the dreaming to get to the freehold where Kim's parents are and from there have them try to figure out who had kidnapped his brother and where he was and why they were holding him. Now OOC, the reason is that a) a number of nobles didn't like Kim's parents marrying and having children, b) they are afraid of Kim, in that he is a Kinain with high glamor and doesn't seem to be affected by the mists, and when he is older and trained in arts and realms could be dangerous to them. Unknown to the characters, Kim has had some training in arts and realms and has had some combat training so that he could protect his brother. Of course, the powers that kidnapped his brother didn't know this. Also, it was Kim starting to act like a normal teenager and have friends (The PCs) and be more active at school and stand out more at school that attracted the others to finding him and his brother. Kim feels it was his fault this has happened, and I want the PCs to feel some responsibility for this also.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T05:45:24-08:00","id":811720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=808987#post808987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For all that C:tD makes hay over the Technocracy being inherently Banal, it's really not. The Technocracy is every fantastic story about exciting spy and technological work. While there are elements of banality to it, they're not nearly so overwhelming as is implied by C:tD, which just associated &quot;Banality&quot; with &quot;Badness.&quot; It's a flaw in C:tD that I hope C20 fixes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The First Precept of Damian aka the code of the Technocracy: &quot;Bring Stasis and order to the Universe. Predictability brings safety. Once all is discovered and all is known, Unity will be Won&quot; Technocrats know Banality is a good thing. Fairies are alien parasites that must be destroyed for the good of Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T06:54:18-08:00","id":811757,"title":"","content":"And yet, the Technocracy has numerous member groups which clearly do not adhere to nor believe in that philosophy, given their ever-forward progress in technological development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T03:17:12-08:00","id":812478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=811757#post811757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, the Technocracy has numerous member groups which clearly do not adhere to nor believe in that philosophy, given their ever-forward progress in technological development.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really? Technological progress is in a direction a goal to achieving a final point they want to achieve the end of History, where progress ends. The Technocracy is not Technology for its own sake. Its making a world without monsters, a world of safety and security for all people. If you want technology for itsown sake.. well there's a reason 2 of those groups left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T06:30:46-08:00","id":812550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=812478#post812478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not really? Technological progress is in a direction a goal to achieving a final point they want to achieve the end of History, where progress ends. The Technocracy is not Technology for its own sake. Its making a world without monsters, a world of safety and security for all people. If you want technology for itsown sake.. well there's a reason 2 of those groups left.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see a nocker or a boggan fitting in with those goals. They can be &quot;people&quot; rather than &quot;monsters&quot; when they're focused on just making things move along. And if you claim Pentex is about &quot;a world without monsters&quot; I'll take you for a tour of their genetics laboratories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T07:28:18-08:00","id":817577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=812550#post812550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could see a nocker or a boggan fitting in with those goals. They can be &quot;people&quot; rather than &quot;monsters&quot; when they're focused on just making things move along. And if you claim Pentex is about &quot;a world without monsters&quot; I'll take you for a tour of their genetics laboratories.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pentex isn't a part of the Technocracy. Its more a sort of dangerously embarassing outgrowth/cancer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T07:59:44-08:00","id":817598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=817577#post817577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Pentex isn't a part of the Technocracy. Its more a sort of dangerously embarassing outgrowth/cancer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh? My mistake, then. Are there not parts of the Technocracy (e.g. Progenitors) who create monsters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:26:10-08:00","id":817627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=817598#post817598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh? My mistake, then. Are there not parts of the Technocracy (e.g. Progenitors) who create monsters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not! Lizardmen, clones, victors these are just necissary technologies like a car or a smart phone.(Yes amazingly a WOD organization has moments of corruption and hypocracy and failure). Either way the Technocracy is about imposing world that has no place for even the most benign of Kithain, that humanity might be &quot;less creative&quot; because of this is just a cost for a safer world.<br /> <br /> OF course from a changeling perspective they are completely wrong, but that goes without saying.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:28:36-08:00","id":817631,"title":"","content":"From the Changeling perspective they may not appreciate the difference between lizardmen and pooka. One just needs to be made aware of the wider reality of the Dreaming, which clearly makes the world safer because not knowing makes you less safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:23:48-08:00","id":817735,"title":"","content":"Am reading &quot;Call to battle&quot; As we speak their ARE INdeed Technocrats who build monsters...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:08:26-08:00","id":818026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=817631#post817631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the Changeling perspective they may not appreciate the difference between lizardmen and pooka. One just needs to be made aware of the wider reality of the Dreaming, which clearly makes the world safer because not knowing makes you less safe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am not trying to argue the morality or objective truth of the Technocracy position. Merely that they actively court banality because they see it as a small price to pay in order to cut off those alien parasite who feed on sleepers(changelings). This their perspective in Mage. They are not glorious champions of free thought and Science as wonder but rather those who try to control the world through science, who winnow down possibilities. They cannot work with fairies except to use them in the short term until they drown in banality there is no long term alliance.<br /> <br /> In mage they are all sorts of questions about how much security is worth vs freedom. In changeling they are the grey men who kill dreams. They transform art into comerce and propaganda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T06:12:32-08:00","id":818369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=818026#post818026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am not trying to argue the morality or objective truth of the Technocracy position. Merely that they actively court banality because they see it as a small price to pay in order to cut off those alien parasite who feed on sleepers(changelings). This their perspective in Mage. They are not glorious champions of free thought and Science as wonder but rather those who try to control the world through science, who winnow down possibilities. They cannot work with fairies except to use them in the short term until they drown in banality there is no long term alliance.<br /> <br /> In mage they are all sorts of questions about how much security is worth vs freedom. In changeling they are the grey men who kill dreams. They transform art into comerce and propaganda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. But the one or two faeries whose methods and motives align in the short term can still show up working for them. Or with them. They may get crushed by the banality, or they may create a metaphorical tumor of creativity and glamour in the organization until somebody changes the &quot;game&quot; from &quot;purge via banality&quot; to &quot;purge with violence&quot; (if the Changeling is winning the &quot;wonder vs. tedium&quot; game).<br /> <br /> The point is that you can, in fact, have one or two working for a Technocracy organization, whether as traitors to Changeling-kind or just because, without it making no sense at all and without one side or the other being a complete dupe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T12:15:50-08:00","id":818628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=818369#post818369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure. But the one or two faeries whose methods and motives align in the short term can still show up working for them. Or with them. They may get crushed by the banality, or they may create a metaphorical tumor of creativity and glamour in the organization until somebody changes the &quot;game&quot; from &quot;purge via banality&quot; to &quot;purge with violence&quot; (if the Changeling is winning the &quot;wonder vs. tedium&quot; game).<br /> <br /> The point is that you can, in fact, have one or two working for a Technocracy organization, whether as traitors to Changeling-kind or just because, without it making no sense at all and without one side or the other being a complete dupe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not really. The Technocracy is pretty brainwashy when you're inside what is properly the Technocracy. Now the Syndicate is more than willing to use temporary disposable assets among other supernaturals but that is pretty much a &quot;dupe&quot; in every sense of the word. <br /> <br /> Really noncrat technomancers are probably the way to go here, along with cutting edge mortal tech companies. Of course the way some companies treat their employees I'd imagine the whole thing is an elaborate Ravaging scheme!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T04:28:06-08:00","id":841816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=817735#post817735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am reading &quot;Call to battle&quot; As we speak their ARE INdeed Technocrats who build monsters...</div> </div> </div> </div>A novel which should be taken with a grain of salt. After all, it has a Garou who is also a Bubasti and can shift into both forms. And that same character can also change into a Khara... double whut?<br /> Call to Battle and Conspicuous Consumption are some of the most head-scratching Werewolf novels out there if you know how things work in W:tA very well.<br /> The author for Conspicuous Consumption even mixed up aspects of the Weaver for the Wyrm...<br /> <br /> None of the events in those two novels were ever confirmed by W:tA Metaplot or RPG books (<i>Whereas the events in the Silver Crown and Breathe Deeply novels are confirmed.</i>).<br /> So yeah, the NPC profile for Passer in Rage: Warriors of the Apocalypse is correct and he never died like he did in Conspicuous Consumption.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the Progenitors don't view what they are creating as &quot;monsters&quot; and neither do the majority of Technocrats view them as doing such. If and that's a big &quot;if&quot;, the Progenitors left or ever got kicked out of the Technocracy, then the Technocracy might view their creations as something they might have to hunt down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T14:53:49-08:00","id":844161,"title":"","content":"you want an EASY idea? Rescue a changeling from autumn people, but this may not be what your looking for as its letting garou become part of a CTD Plot rather then incorporating changelings into a WTA Plot<br /> <br /> But garou are not vulnerable to Banality, so would make invaluable allies for such a mission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T19:10:28-08:00","id":844271,"title":"","content":"Thanks Prince of the Night, having a plot involving Autumn People would be something very different. This is a very interesting idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T02:22:53-08:00","id":844405,"title":"","content":"Autumn People might, in their blindness, theoretically go after Garou too, thinking them kin to the fae.<br /> <br /> The new MET WTA also suggests another possibility: trying to lift the Samhain Queen's curse on the Fianna. Or otherwise using the curse as a plot point to introduce the fae.<br /> <br /> By the way, in a WTA game, I'd let changelings soak aggravated damaged (as per CTD ST's Guide, this is an optional but widely used rule, which the corebook encourages). You should probably also use the Unleashing rules revealed in the C20 KS previews, to give them a more mysterious and formidable way with magic than the Arts and Realms system normally allows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 03-09-2016, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T06:30:02-08:00","id":844473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=844405#post844405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Autumn People might, in their blindness, theoretically go after Garou too, thinking them kin to the fae.<br /> <br /> The new MET WTA also suggests another possibility: trying to lift the Samhain Queen's curse on the Fianna. Or otherwise using the curse as a plot point to introduce the fae.<br /> <br /> By the way, in a WTA game, I'd let changelings soak aggravated damaged (as per CTD ST's Guide, this is an optional but widely used rule, which the corebook encourages). You should probably also use the Unleashing rules revealed in the C20 KS previews, to give them a more mysterious and formidable way with magic than the Arts and Realms system normally allows.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dauntain, perhaps, but What about Heavy Sleepers, or Autumn Fae? <br /> <br /> Hmmmn, how many employees of DNA or Pentex ARE Heavy Sleepers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T13:51:46-08:00","id":844713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/806305-ideas-for-using-changelins-in-w-ta-game?p=844473#post844473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Dauntain, perhaps, but What about Heavy Sleepers, or Autumn Fae?<br /> <br /> Hmmmn, how many employees of DNA or Pentex ARE Heavy Sleepers?</div> </div> </div> </div>DNA and Pentex are going to have lots of really heavy sleepers all around. The former thinks that it can explain everything about the Garou with orthodox principles of just the physical world, while Pentex's corporate policies are geared toward crushing the spirits of employees under mountains of paperwork and persistent demands from managers for them to come in one Saturday, yeah, that'd be great, thanks, and don't forget about those TPS cover sheets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T15:47:32-08:00","id":844773,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the ideas for other adventures, but what about my OP. I need ideas on taking the group to Ireland to help Kim. Any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T23:44:19-08:00","id":845497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>David G</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/fo